      "pass": true,
      "value": "R42 browser success did not make its geometry successful: persisted QA shows zero incremental gain. The first R43 attempt also produced zero gain, proving that two-sided same-row gap closure was not an available repair class. A second diagnostic error was treating row-run count or rowRuns/active as a necessary fragmentation truth after R41 deliberately introduced adjacent-row branches. Legitimate branches can add row runs, and rowRuns/active can be gamed downward simply by appending cells to existing runs without reconnecting topology. R43 therefore keeps those values as diagnostics but gates fragmentation with same-family/stair-compatible 2-D connected components, tiny components and orphan cells, while the actual geometry work remains one frozen-source branch companion rather than riser amplification or global mask closing.",
